        'notes' => [
            'Urea: fixed MRP with a floating subsidy (70–80% of realisation) designed to give a 12% post-tax RoE on fixed costs; units are grouped on energy norms of 5.5, 6.0 and 6.5 Gcal/MT. Geographic diversification is not a key factor for urea (offtake assured up to re-assessed capacity).',
            'P&K: floating MRP with a fixed nutrient-based subsidy (about 30% of realisation) set roughly every six months; DoF caps PBT at 8% for traders, 10% for manufacturers and 12% for integrated manufacturers.',
            'Working capital borrowings fund sovereign subsidy receivables, so interest coverage is the key coverage measure; DSCR matters for plants with term debt. The adequacy of the subsidy budget is a key monitorable.',
